      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-96475",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = (x - 1)(y + 2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x, y)$ where $x > 1$ and $y > - 2$, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point $(x, y)$ where $x < 1$ and $y > - 2$, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point $(x, y)$ where $x > 1$ and $y < - 2$, the slope of the slope field is positive"
